quran[18]{c,v,t}:
  52,32,Or do their minds prompt them to say this (foolish thing)? Or are they (just) rebellious people?
  52,33,"Or do they say: ‘He has forged it (i.e. the Qur’an)’? Instead, they do not believe (in the truth)."
  52,34,Let them bring a discourse like this (Qur’an) if they are truthful.
  52,35,Or were they created from nothing? Or are they (their own) creators?
  52,36,"Did they create the heavens and the earth? Instead, they are not certain (about anything)."
  52,37,Or do they possess the treasures of your Lord? Or are they the controllers (of its distribution)?
  52,38,"Or do they have a ladder (leading up to heaven) whereby they can listen? Then, let their listener produce a manifest authority."
  52,39,Or does He have daughters while you have sons?
  52,40,Or do you ask them (O Prophet!) for a reward (for conveying the message) such that they are overburdened with debt?
  52,41,Or do they have (knowledge of) the Unseen that they write down?
  52,42,"Or do they desire to scheme (against you, O Prophet)? Then, the disbelievers themselves shall be the victims of (their) schemes."
  52,43,Or do they have any god besides Allah? Glory be to Allah from the partners they ascribe (to Him).
  52,44,"Even if they saw a fragment falling from the sky, they would say: ‘(This is just) a heap of layered clouds.’"
  52,45,"So leave them until they encounter their Day, in which they will be thunderstruck,"
  52,46,"the Day when their scheming will not avail them in any way, nor will they be helped."
  52,47,"Indeed, for the wrongdoers, there is a punishment besides that, but most of them do not know."
  52,48,"So submit patiently to the judgement of your Lord, for indeed you are before Our Eyes (all the time). And glorify the praise of your Lord when you rise (at dawn)."
  52,49,And glorify Him during the night and at the setting of the stars.
